.TH "SERIALPORT.GETINFO" "3JS" "May 19, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
SerialPort.getInfo \- SerialPort: getInfo() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Dedicated Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]getInfo()\f[B]\f[R] method of the \f[CR]SerialPort\f[R]
interface returns an object containing identifying information for the
device available via the port.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
getInfo()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
An object containing the following properties:
.TP
\f[B]usbVendorId\f[R]
If the port is part of a USB device, this property is a positive integer
that identifies the device\(cqs vendor.
If not, it is \f[CR]undefined\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]usbProductId\f[R]
If the port is part of a USB device, this property is a positive integer
that identifies the USB device.
If not, it is \f[CR]undefined\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]bluetoothServiceClassId\f[R] \f[I](experimental)\f[R]
If the port is a Bluetooth RFCOMM service, this property is a positive
integer or string representing the device\(cqs Bluetooth service class
ID.
If not, it is \f[CR]undefined\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Get information from a selected device
This snippet calls the \f[CR]Serial.requestPort()\f[R] method when a
\f[CR]<button>\f[R] is pressed.
We pass a filter to \f[CR]requestPort()\f[R] to filter for Arduino Uno
USB devices.
Once a port is requested, we call \f[CR]getInfo()\f[R] to return the
device\(cqs \f[CR]usbProductId\f[R] and \f[CR]usbVendorId\f[R].
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]button\f[R] id=\(dqconnect\(dq>Connect</\f[B]button\f[R]>
.EE
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] connectBtn = document.getElementById(\(dqconnect\(dq);

\f[I]// Filter for devices with the Arduino Uno USB Vendor/Product IDs\f[R]
\f[B]const\f[R] filters = [
  { usbVendorId: 0x2341, usbProductId: 0x0043 },
  { usbVendorId: 0x2341, usbProductId: 0x0001 },
];

connectBtn.addEventListener(\(dqclick\(dq, \f[B]async\f[R] () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[B]try\f[R] {
    \f[I]// Prompt the user to select an Arduino Uno device\f[R]
    \f[B]const\f[R] port = \f[B]await\f[R] navigator.serial.requestPort({ filters });

    \f[I]// Return the device\(aqs identifying info\f[R]
    \f[B]const\f[R] { usbProductId, usbVendorId } = port.getInfo();
  } \f[B]catch\f[R] (e) {
    \f[I]// The user didn\(aqt select a device\f[R]
  }
});
.EE
